Third-party bundled assets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Twemoji (assets/twemoji/*.svg)
------------------------------
The emoji graphics bundled under `assets/twemoji/` are from the Twemoji
project and are used as the default, platform-uniform emoji glyph set.

  Copyright 2020 Twitter, Inc and other contributors
  Graphics licensed under CC-BY 4.0:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Source: https://github.com/jdecked/twemoji

CC-BY 4.0 requires attribution. This NOTICE, together with the credit in the
README, provides that attribution. If you swap the default `EmojiRenderer`
away from Twemoji (e.g. to native OS glyphs via `defaultEmojiRenderer`, or to
your own uniform set), the Twemoji attribution requirement no longer applies
to your build.

Starter stickers (assets/stickers/*.svg, assets/stickers/*.json)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Original works created for refraction_ui, licensed under the package's MIT
License. These are a small starter pack; hosts supply their own via the
`RefractionEmojiPicker.stickers` seam.

Animated Noto emoji (assets/emoji_animated/*.json)
---------------------------------------------------
The Lottie animations bundled under `assets/emoji_animated/` (one file per
key in `tool/animated_emoji.txt`) are Google's animated Noto emoji, fetched
unmodified from the official catalogue's CDN
(fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/latest/<codepoint>/lottie.json) by
`tool/fetch_animated_emoji.dart`.

  "Noto Animated Emoji" by Google, licensed under CC BY 4.0:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Source: https://googlefonts.github.io/noto-emoji-animation/
  No changes were made to the animations.

CC BY 4.0 requires attribution. This NOTICE, together with the credit in the
README, provides it. An app that ships `refraction_ui` and displays these
animations (jumbo emoji-only chat messages in `RefractionChatBubble`) must keep
an equivalent credit in its own licence/attribution screen; Flutter's
`LicenseRegistry` does not pick up asset licences automatically.

Note: the animated set is licensed separately from the static Noto Color Emoji
font (SIL OFL 1.1) and the noto-emoji repository's tooling (Apache 2.0). An
earlier version of this NOTICE cited those licences for these files; that was
wrong. CC BY 4.0 is the licence that applies to the animations.
